        "quote": "(a) It shall be the duty of every person constructing, owning, maintaining or operating any railroad within the City to keep the tracks of such railroad free and unobstructed so as not to interfere with public traffic upon the streets, avenues and alleys of the City; provided, that such person may stand cars upon such tracks in alleys during such times as may be reasonably required for loading and unloading such cars, but no longer.",
